From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: mark the fbdev framebuffer as system memory

Backport the upstream framebuffer flag fix for Armada's 7.2.6 kernel.
The Yoga Slim 7x boot captures report sys_imageblit and sys_fillrect
rejecting the framebuffer after the MSM console handoff. The MSM fbdev
buffer uses a kernel virtual mapping and needs FBINFO_VIRTFB.

Link: https://lkml.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2607.3/13309.html
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
@@ -132,6 +132,7 @@
 	helper->fb = fb;
 
 	fbi->fbops = &msm_fb_ops;
+	fbi->flags |= FBINFO_VIRTFB; /* system memory */
 
 	drm_fb_helper_fill_info(fbi, helper, sizes);
 
